<title>GERMANY: E.German Sept industry output falls 3.4 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>E.German Sept industry output falls 3.4 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> E.GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT   Sept 96     Aug 96     Sept 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change (pct)  -3.4	 +6.1	  -4.1</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +1.8	 +1.1	   n/a</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)	     141.5	146.5	 139.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbnk statistics. Previously reported data in brackets.  </p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				    Sept 96	     Aug 96</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Manufacturing output   156.2	-3.6     162.0	 +9.2</p>
<p>Including:</p>
<p>  Intermediate goods    182.5	-6.3     194.7	 +5.4</p>
<p>  Capital goods	   127.6	-7.9     138.6	+16.1</p>
<p> Energy output	     86.7	-2.0	88.5	 -1.4</p>
<p> Construction	     200.3	-3.4     207.3	 +4.0</p>
<p>Two month comparison Aug/Sept 96 with June/July 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output			 +1.0</p>
<p>Two month comparison Aug/Sept 96 with Aug/Sept 95:</p>
<p> Industrial output			 +0.6</p>
<p> Mining					-7.8</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		   +4.6</p>
<p>  Including:Intermediate goods	 +4.9</p>
<p>		Capital goods		-0.8</p>
<p>		Consumer durables	 -12.1</p>
<p>		Consumer goods	    +17.6</p>
<p> Energy output			     +0.8</p>
<p> Construction				-5.0</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn Newsroom, 49-28-26097150</p>
